+# Serial RSpec profiling: models and requests
 
 Run from the repository root, with the normal test database and Redis running:
 
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ A second order (seed 4321) passed all 1,795 examples in 53.73s.
   records or their associations: rolling back SQL doesn't reset Ruby objects.
   Don't share Redis state, job queues, or files that examples modify this way.
 
-## Next measurement
+## Model phase handoff
 
 After these changes, `MediaAttachment` was the slowest file (6.4s): audio
 cover art and thumbnail specs really do need file processing. Keep those
@@ -51,3 +51,64 @@ Profile `spec/requests` separately before changing it. Do not assume that fake
 jobs are appropriate there: a request can check downstream effects across
 models. Add the two separately measured serial times to track the combined
 speedup. This phase did not benchmark requests or change fabricators.
+
+## Request phase
+
+```sh
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --seed 1234 --profile 15
+```
+
+The model phase recorded no request time. The request-only starting point
+measured here was **199.5s for 1,877 examples, 0 failures**. The model phase's
+file-scoped changes do not apply in a request-only run. Use the same default
+filters; these figures do not include streaming, search or JS examples.
+
+The slowest 15 examples accounted for only 7.9% of the baseline. Rank files by
+**total** example time, not average time (and save a copy before rerunning).
+These totals locate hotspots; use `Finished in` for the comparison, because
+per-example timings do not include all of the shared group setup:
+
+```sh
+awk -F'|' '/^\.\/spec\/requests\// { split($1, id, /\[/); t[id[1]] += $3 } END { for (f in t) printf "%.2f %s\n", t[f], f }' tmp/rspec/examples.txt | sort -nr | head -15
+```
+
+- `cache_spec` consumed 38.4s. Its 258 examples need independent HTTP sessions,
+  headers, settings, caches and requests, but not 258 copies of the same rows.
+  Only the database setup is shared. The outbox, reply and public timeline
+  matrices use the same principle. Replies alone cost 19.5s; keep suspension,
+  visibility, blocks and extra pagination rows local to each example.
+- The v1/v2 notification files took 17.3s together. Build the notification
+  history once per endpoint group in a transaction. Run the real posting,
+  follow, favourite and delivery code there, and refetch users before each
+  example. Keep the tokens, read markers, clears and request parameters local.
+  Don't move the normal cache/Redis cleanup into a group hook.
+- A blanket fake-Sidekiq trial broke 13 examples, including conversations,
+  home timelines and unfavouriting. Keep the request default inline: some
+  endpoints assert the **result** of a job, even when there is no explicit
+  job expectation. A `before_all` hook runs outside per-example job settings;
+  explicitly select inline mode there when the fixture needs delivery.
+- Signature verification spent 8.8s across 30 examples, each redrawing and
+  then reloading the entire application router. Use Rails' `with_routing` for
+  temporary endpoints: it restores the original route set after each example
+  without reloading `config/routes.rb`. The CSP test uses the same helper.
+- For pagination, exercise both sides of a limit without fabricating a full
+  production-sized page. The slowest baseline example (3.02s) needed a next
+  link for an ActivityPub context; it still fills a page, at a test-local limit.
+
+### Serial comparison (seed 1234, excluding load)
+
+| Group | Baseline (s) | Optimized (s) | Examples | Failures |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Requests | 199.50 | 116.00 | 1,877 | 0 |
+| Models (previous phase) | 170.20 | 53.19 | 1,795 | 0 |
+| Sum of separate runs | 369.70 | 169.19 | 3,672 | 0 |
+
+Requests took 41.9% less time (1.72× speedup); the combined speedup is 2.19×.
+For orientation, final per-example totals were 5.0s for the cache matrix,
+4.2s for replies, 2.4s for v1/v2 notifications together, and 0.85s for
+signature verification. No request authentication shortcuts or fabricator
+changes were needed.
+
+Isolation check: reran the changed request groups at seed 4321 (418 examples,
+0 failures, 17.84s), including repeated visibility changes, notification
+clears, alternate authentication modes and temporary route sets.
